{"page":2,"totalPages":3,"perPage":6,"nextPage":3,"html":"<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/task-board.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/task-board.webp\" alt=\"A kanban board with cards spread across To Do, In Progress and Done\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-03-22T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.03.22</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/task-management\">Task management app</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A lightweight, visual task board that runs entirely in the browser. Move work between columns, track what is in flight, and keep day-to-day planning low friction: no backend, no account, nothing to sync.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>React</li><li>Productivity</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/balanced-tree.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/balanced-tree.webp\" alt=\"A balanced binary tree built from twelve values, each node labelled with its height\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2020-04-09T00:00:00.000Z\">2020.04.09</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>2 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/balanced-tree\">Balanced binary tree animated</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Balanced binary trees promise fast inserts, finds and deletes, and rotations are what keep the promise: they stop the tree from growing lopsided. Add and remove nodes here and watch each rotation play out one step at a time.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>CSS</li><li>Balanced Binary Tree</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/minesweeper.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/minesweeper.webp\" alt=\"An expert minesweeper board most of the way played out, with flagged mines\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2020-02-18T00:00:00.000Z\">2020.02.18</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/minesweeper\">Minesweeper</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">The classic sweep-for-mines game, rebuilt with React and plain CSS on top of a flood fill that opens up the empty regions. Same nerve-wracking first click, now with a seven-segment timer counting against you.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Minesweeper</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/todo-board.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/todo-board.webp\" alt=\"A three column todo board with items spread across Todo, Doing and Done\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2020-01-26T00:00:00.000Z\">2020.01.26</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/reacttodolist\">Todo list with React and LocalStorage</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A todo list that lives entirely in your browser: React for the interface, localStorage for memory. Close the tab, come back next week, and the list is exactly where you left it.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>React</li><li>CSS</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/sudoku-solver.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/sudoku-solver.webp\" alt=\"A sudoku grid solved in the browser, with the solver’s digits picked out from the given ones\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2017-07-02T00:00:00.000Z\">2017.07.02</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/sudokusolver\">Sudoku solver</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A randomized constraint solver for Sudoku, ported from Python to JavaScript so it runs as you watch. Hand it a puzzle with more than one solution and it will cheerfully give you a different answer each time.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Sudoku</li><li>Computing</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/orbit-camera.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/orbit-camera.webp\" alt=\"Coloured spheres over a mountain skybox, seen through the orbit camera\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2016-08-13T00:00:00.000Z\">2016.08.13</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>2 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/orbit-camera\">Orbit Camera for 3D scenes</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Most orbit controls rotate around a fixed origin, which starts to feel wrong the moment you zoom in on something off-centre. These controls pick whatever sits under your cursor as the object of interest and orbit around that instead.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>3D</li><li>camera</li><li>orbit</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>"}